## Section 4. Materials Storage

tutorial-tide-sg-find-locked-door = Go to the bolted door.

tutorial-tide-sg-open-panel = Open the door's wire panel.
tutorial-tide-control-open-panel = Use a screwdriver on the door to open its panel.
tutorial-tide-him-open-panel-1 = Right. Now look over here.
tutorial-tide-him-open-panel-2 = Engineering keeps materials in there.
tutorial-tide-him-open-panel-3 = Let's take some, they'll never miss it.
tutorial-tide-him-open-panel-4 = Screwdriver. Panel on the side. Every airlock's has one.
tutorial-tide-him-open-panel-5 = You're not breaking it. You're opening it.
tutorial-tide-him-open-panel-6 = There's a difference, and Security doesn't care about the difference, so be quick.

tutorial-tide-sg-cut-power = Cut the door's power.
tutorial-tide-control-cut-power = Cut the door's power wires with the wirecutter.
tutorial-tide-him-cut-power-1 = Now let's cut some wires.
tutorial-tide-him-cut-power-2 = You don't know which one's are which. The colors are always different. You gotta guess.
tutorial-tide-him-cut-power-3 = Two of them are power, one's main and one's backup.
tutorial-tide-him-cut-power-4 = Start cutting.

tutorial-tide-sg-restore-power = Reconnect every cut wire.
tutorial-tide-control-restore-power = Use the wirecutters on every cut wire to mend it.
tutorial-tide-him-restore-power-1 = Right, it was bolted.
tutorial-tide-him-restore-power-2 = You can't move bolts without electricity. Reconnect all the wires.
tutorial-tide-him-restore-power-3 = We need to pulse the bolt. A cut wire can't be pulsed.

tutorial-tide-sg-unbolt-door = Get the bolts up.
tutorial-tide-control-unbolt-door = Use a multitool on the wires until you find the bolt wire.
tutorial-tide-him-unbolt-door-1 = Now use the multitool. Pulse the wires until the bolt light goes away.
tutorial-tide-him-unbolt-door-2 = Bolts are motors, and motors need power. That's why we put back the wires.

tutorial-tide-him-unbolt-door-retry = You pulsed a power wire... Cut and reconnect it, or wait until it resets.

tutorial-tide-sg-cut-power-again = Take the power off it again.
tutorial-tide-control-cut-power-again = Cut the power wires again with the wirecutter.
tutorial-tide-him-cut-power-again-1 = Bolts are gone. Now we can depower it.
tutorial-tide-him-cut-power-again-2 = Cut both power wires again. Remember which ones?

tutorial-tide-sg-pry-door = Pry the door open.
tutorial-tide-control-pry-door = Use a crowbar on the door to pry it open.
tutorial-tide-him-pry-door-1 = Well done. You're a natural.
tutorial-tide-him-pry-door-2 = There it is. Took you what, a minute? Two?
tutorial-tide-him-pry-door-3 = Now use the crowbar to open it.

tutorial-tide-sg-take-steel = Take some steel.
tutorial-tide-him-take-steel-1 = Steel. Take a stack.
tutorial-tide-him-take-steel-2 = Not because I've got a plan. I never have a plan.
tutorial-tide-him-take-steel-3 = Well, maybe I've got a bit of a plan.
tutorial-tide-him-take-steel-4 = Right. Bring it.
tutorial-tide-him-take-steel-5 = Follow me.

