tutorial-tide-him-open-construction-5 = Let's lay some pipe.

tutorial-tide-sg-place-pipe = Lay the first length of pipe.
tutorial-tide-control-place-pipe = Find "disposal pipe segment" under "Utilities" and place a construction ghost. You can rotate the ghost with [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="EditorRotateObject"][/bold][/color]. Then close the construction menu and exit build mode with [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="EditorCancelPlace"][/bold][/color]. Then put the steel in your hand and click on the green construction ghosts you placed to start construction.
tutorial-tide-him-place-pipe-1 = The straigh pieces. Not the fancy ones.
tutorial-tide-him-place-pipe-2 = You don't want a junction, you don't want a signaller, and you definitely don't want whatever a router is.
tutorial-tide-him-place-pipe-3 = Line it up with the ones already there.

tutorial-tide-sg-build-pipe = Lay the second length.
tutorial-tide-control-build-pipe = Do the same again for the second gap.
tutorial-tide-him-build-pipe-1 = And the other one. That's it.
tutorial-tide-him-build-pipe-2 = Four steel and a bit of patience, and now there's a way into a room there wasn't a way into.
tutorial-tide-him-build-pipe-3 = Can you believe it?

tutorial-tide-sg-get-in-bin = Get into the disposal unit.
tutorial-tide-control-get-in-bin = Drag yourself onto the disposal unit, or right-click it and pick Enter.
tutorial-tide-him-get-in-bin-1 = Right.
tutorial-tide-him-get-in-bin-2 = Get into the bin.
tutorial-tide-him-get-in-bin-3 = The corporate one told you not to get in the bin, didn't she.
tutorial-tide-him-get-in-bin-4 = Yeah. She tells everyone that.
tutorial-tide-him-get-in-bin-5 = Get in the bin.

